Wipemark
Copyright 2026 Wipemark contributors

Third-party material redistributed inside the Wipemark binary and its
installers. This file covers *bundled assets and vendored source*, not
the full Cargo dependency graph — `cargo license` over `Cargo.lock` is
the authority on that, and epic E10 wires it into the packaging step.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Icons
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The SVG files in `apps/wipemark-app/assets/icons/` are sourced from
Font Awesome Free, Solid style, version 7.2.0.

  Copyright Fonticons, Inc. (https://fontawesome.com)
  Icons: CC BY 4.0 License
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  https://fontawesome.com/license/free

They are embedded verbatim into the executable by rust-embed and each
file retains the Font Awesome attribution comment inline, as authored —
that comment is the attribution CC BY 4.0 asks for, and this file is
the second copy of it. The committed set is a curated subset; the
canonical list is the directory itself. Two files are renamed and not
otherwise changed: `close.svg` is Font Awesome's `xmark.svg`, and
`eye-off.svg` is its `eye-slash.svg`.

Nothing here is Font Awesome Pro. The full Free corpus is the public
`@fortawesome/fontawesome-free` npm package, pulled into `dev-staging/`
when a glyph is promoted; `scripts/promote-icon.sh` refuses a file that
does not carry the Free attribution, and `every_icon_is_a_free_glyph`
in `apps/wipemark-app/src/icon.rs` checks the committed set. The
workflow is documented in `docs/architecture/icons.md`.

The application icon under `apps/wipemark-app/assets/icon/` and
`icons/` is original work, generated by `icons/create-icons.sh` from
`icons/watermark-broom.svg`. It is not FontAwesome material.

